        "timestamp": 1773741487,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Why is Trump looking to China to help open the Strait of Hormuz? Issued on: 17/03/2026 - 10:58 US president Donald Trump has called on numerous nations, including China, to help ships safely ‌transit the key Strait of Hormuz, where one-fifth of the world's oil transits on a daily basis. But why has Trump turned to Beijing, so often an adversary of the US and ally of Iran, for help? France 24's Olvier Farry takes a look. US embassy in Baghdad attacked as Iraq pulled deeper into Mideast war 17/03/2026 'Like buying a ticket to the Titanic': EU leaders reject Trump's Hormuz demands 17/03/2026 'Macron alone in his tower': No candidates defending his govt or mandate in France's local elections 17/03/2026 France Ghassan Salamé urges Israel and international community to let Lebanon 'do Its job more efficiently' 17/03/2026 Middle East China overlooks Trump's demands for Hormuz strait, calls for all sides to de-escalate 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli campaign in Lebanon seeks to 'degrade' Hezbollah’s rocket, drone and missile capabilities 16/03/2026 Middle East 'Near universal refusal' - European leaders reject Trump's demand for Strait of Hormuz mission 16/03/2026 Middle East Iran's underground arsenal, decentralised military key to press on with strikes on Gulf states 16/03/2026 Middle East Missiles and drone attacks across the UAE as Iran presses on with air campaign in Gulf 16/03/2026 Middle East"
